      "statusChangeNewStatus": "interested",
      "value": "Hey all, as part of the increased streamlining and internal organization efforts we're putting towards collecting feedback without letting it fall through the cracks this one got tagged as \"in progress\" a bit early. (I was planning to handle the tagging myself but it's also on a list that Scout among others have been working through to make sure stuff isn't missed).\nSorry about the confusion so here's a super detailed status update on it:\nWhen we first introduced Horizon Adjust there was some concern in the team that it would be used as a distracting toy in a way that detracts from the vibe world creators work to express in their worlds. Since release though we've had time to gather info on the impact enough that those concerns within the team have reduced. \nIn other words, I have the go-ahead now to start internal testing on ways to address this feedback for the need for fine-tuning! The current status is at pre-internal-testing stage, and it could be the case that during internal testing stuff comes up that prevents it moving forward, but I'm hopeful we'll have something to show eventually.\nSo for now I'm marking this as \"interested\" because I think that better reflects the current status but technically it is in progress. I'll keep the tags updated with status comments as it moves along!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
